    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d706">

                <pb facs="0780" n="672" xml:id="pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5131/556: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-09-10T11:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 10,
                                1927—11 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>268. Department desires that you present draft treaty immediately and inform
                    French Foreign Office that this Government is ready to begin
                        negotiations.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d706-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d706-f1" n="65" xml:id="d706-f1-content">
                <p>On Sept. 12, 5 p.m., the Chargé telegraphed: “346. Have just handed in draft of
                    treaty to the Foreign Office. Whitehouse.” (File No. 611.5131/558.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
